# tj-lhos-panel — core rules

You are building a **single-user personal super-agent dashboard** ("Grok-style")
on **Next.js 16 (App Router, TypeScript)** — frontend **and** backend in one app,
Dockerized, fronted by the existing Caddy on the host.

## Before writing any code
- Read `docs/CONTEXT.md` (master context), `TODO.md` (current phase), `CHANGELOG.md`.
- The backend integrates with an existing, running system — **do not mock it**:
  - LHOS REST API + MCP server: see `docs/API_REFERENCE.md`, `docs/MCP_REFERENCE.md`
  - Endpoints base: `https://mcp.hostx.h22t.com` (REST under `/api/*`, MCP at `/mcp`)
  - Live VNC desktop: `https://vnc.hostx.h22t.com/` (see `docs/INTEGRATIONS.md` §VNC)

## Stack decisions (fixed — do not re-litigate)
- Next.js 16 App Router + TypeScript strict; Node runtime for API routes (not edge).
- DB: **PostgreSQL + pgvector** via Drizzle ORM. Schema in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- Realtime: Server-Sent Events (SSE) for chat streaming + usage ticker; no socket.io.
- State: Zustand (client), TanStack Query (server cache).
- Styling: Tailwind v4 + CSS variables from `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`. No component
  library theme defaults — we have our own design language.
- Animation: Motion (framer-motion successor) + CSS; sound via small WebAudio helper.
- Auth: single-owner credential login (email+password+TOTP optional) with iron-session
  or Auth.js Credentials — owner only, registration disabled.
- Global settings → `.env` / `.env.local`; runtime-editable settings → DB + JSON
  schema validation from `config/settings.schema.json`; model list → `config/models.json`.

## Hard rules
- **Never hardcode tokens/keys.** All secrets come from env. `.env.local` is produced
  by `scripts/sync-env.sh`. If an env var is missing, fail loudly with a clear message.
- **The browser never receives LHOS/vendor API keys.** All vendor + LHOS calls go
  through Next.js API routes (`/app/api/*`).
- Reusable components live in `src/components/ui/*`; never duplicate a pattern twice —
  extract on second use.
- Every feature you finish: tick it in `TODO.md` and add a line to `CHANGELOG.md`.
- Irreversible agent actions (post/send/pay/delete) must round-trip the **approval
  system** (`docs/skills/skill-approvals-hitl.md`). Never auto-approve.
- Keep LHOS pace/rate-limits: this platform does plain automation of the owner's own
  accounts; do not build anti-detection / bot-evasion behavior of any kind.
